Extend EnemyAI with coordinated squads and attack waves using the existing AI state machine.

  Enemy units should no longer always walk toward the player base immediately after recruitment.
  Implement:

  - A rally point near the enemy base
  - Assignment of available units to a forming attack squad
  - A configurable minimum squad strength and maximum rally wait time
  - A preferred mixed composition of frontline swordsmen and rear-line archers
  - Formation destinations with swordsmen generally ahead of archers
  - A transition from RALLYING to ATTACKING when the squad is ready or has waited too long
  - A clear attack objective, normally the player base, with sensible responses to encountered defenders
  - A transition to RECOVERING when an attack wave has suffered substantial losses
  - Cleanup of squad membership when units die
  - A later return to BUILDING or RALLYING for the next wave

  Avoid requiring every unit to reach an exact formation coordinate, since that can stall an attack. Keep
  thresholds and timings as named configuration values.

  Add deterministic tests covering:

  - New units rallying instead of immediately attacking
  - Formation roles being assigned correctly
  - A sufficiently strong squad launching an attack
  - Maximum rally time preventing permanent waiting
  - Squad members advancing together within a reasonable tolerance
  - Casualties triggering recovery
  - Dead units being removed from squad bookkeeping
  - Successive attack waves being possible

  After implementation:

  1. Run the full automated test suite.
  2. Run a syntax or compilation check.
  3. Simulate enough game time to observe at least two attack waves.
  4. Manually verify that formations do not stall, overlap excessively, or split apart without reason.
  5. Verify that combat targeting and archer kiting still work during a wave.
  6. Take screenshots only under /work/screenshots, inspect each with view_image, and report visual
  problems.
  7. Report state transitions, wave composition, timings, and any balance concerns.

  Do not add adaptive production or full base-defense recalls yet. Do not commit changes.
